counter-terror police were waiting at  luton airport for a man they had wanted  to question for seven years  ain davis who's 38 had been deported  from turkey he was arrested and within  hours was charged with terror  crimes he appeared at westminster  magistrate court where his original  arrest warrant was issued in 2015.  davis is charged with possessing a  firearm for terror purposes  and two charges of arranging terrorism  funding it was a 15-minute hearing in  the dock davis was dressed in a prison  issue grey tracksuit he stood briefly  hands behind his back to confirm his  name he wasn't asked how he wanted to  plead to the charges  in syria davis is alleged to have been a  member of a kidnap gang who took western  hostages and killed some of them  the gang's captives nicknamed the four  isis fighters the beatles because of  their english accents  british aid volunteer alan henning was  allegedly beheaded by the gang so too  was another uk volunteer david haynes  davis has always denied being one of the  gang members  he was held in custody and will appear  at the old bailey next month martin  brunt sky news westminster magistrates  court
 

